  "facts": [
    "Opened on December 26, 2009, the Tianxingzhou Yangtze River Bridge cost CN¥11 billion and stretched 4,657 meters, linking Wuhan’s Third Ring Road to the high‑speed rail network.",
    "Featuring a 504‑meter main span, the Tianxingzhou Yangtze River Bridge holds the world record for the longest combined road and rail cable‑stayed span, surpassing all predecessors.",
    "High‑speed trains cross the river at up to 250 km/h on the bridge, enabling eastern Hefei‑Wuhan services to reach Wuhan railway station directly instead of detouring to Hankou."
